      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Text:\n\"Machine learning algorithms learn patterns from data. Supervised learning uses labeled examples. \nThe model learns to predict targets from features. Regularization prevents overfitting by \npenalizing complex models. Cross-validation estimates generalization performance.\"\n\nPrompt:\nExtract the 2 most important sentences from the text above.\n---\n\nResponse:\n1. \"Machine learning algorithms learn patterns from data.\"\n2. \"Regularization prevents overfitting by penalizing complex models.\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Text:\n[Same as above]\n\nPrompt:\nSummarize the above text in 1-2 sentences, using your own words.\n---\n\nResponse:\n\"Machine learning systems learn patterns from labeled data, with regularization and \ncross-validation helping ensure they generalize well to new data.\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nWrite a 1-sentence executive summary suitable for a C-level executive who needs \nto quickly understand the key business impact.\n\nDocument: [earnings report with 20 pages of financial data]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n\"Q3 revenue grew 15% year-over-year to $2.8B, driven by 22% growth in cloud services \noffsetting an 8% decline in legacy products.\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nSummarize this research paper for a technical audience in 3-4 paragraphs. \nInclude key methodology, results, and implications. Preserve specific metrics and findings.\n\nPaper: [research paper on neural networks]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n\"This paper proposes a novel attention mechanism combining multi-head self-attention \nwith adaptive routing, achieving 12% improvement on ImageNet classification. The \narchitecture uses 42M parameters and trains in 3.2 hours on 8 V100 GPUs. \nWe observed that... [specific technical details preserved]\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nExplain the main ideas of this article in simple language for someone with no background \nin the topic. Use an analogy to make it relatable.\n\nArticle: [physics article about quantum entanglement]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n\"Imagine two magic coins: whenever you flip one and get heads, the other instantly shows \ntails, no matter how far apart they are. That's quantum entanglement\u2014particles connected \nso their properties are linked even across vast distances, which Einstein found spooky \nbut modern physics confirms happens.\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nI'll ask you to write progressively denser summaries. \n\nStep 1: Write a 1-sentence summary.\nStep 2: Write a 2-3 sentence summary adding more details.\nStep 3: Write a 3-5 sentence summary with even more specifics.\n\nDocument: [business report]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n\nStep 1: \"The company increased quarterly revenue by 18% despite supply chain challenges.\"\n\nStep 2: \"The company increased quarterly revenue by 18% to $5.2B, despite supply chain \nchallenges in semiconductors. Operating margins improved from 22% to 24% through cost \noptimization, while R&D investment in AI products grew 35%.\"\n\nStep 3: \"The company increased quarterly revenue by 18% to $5.2B, driven by 22% growth \nin cloud services and 14% in hardware. Operating margins improved from 22% to 24% \nthrough $120M in cost optimization and supply chain efficiency. R&D investment in \nAI products grew 35% to $800M. However, legacy products declined 6%. Guidance for \nnext quarter projects 12-14% growth assuming no further supply disruptions.\""
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nAnalyze the strategic positioning of Company X using SWOT framework:\n- Strengths: What is Company X good at?\n- Weaknesses: What are internal limitations?\n- Opportunities: What external factors could benefit them?\n- Threats: What external risks exist?\n\n[Company description/document]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\nStrengths:\n- Market leadership in cloud infrastructure (40% market share)\n- Strong brand and customer loyalty (NPS of 72)\n- Vertical integration reducing costs\n\nWeaknesses:\n- Legacy systems limiting speed of innovation\n- Limited presence in Asia-Pacific (only 8% revenue)\n- High customer acquisition cost ($15K average)\n\nOpportunities:\n- Growing AI/ML market (35% annual growth)\n- Emerging markets with low penetration\n- Enterprise migration to cloud accelerating\n\nThreats:\n- Intensifying competition from new entrants\n- Potential regulatory constraints on data handling\n- Currency fluctuations affecting international revenue"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nAnalyze this customer feedback using this framework:\n1. What is the core problem?\n2. What are root causes?\n3. What are immediate impacts?\n4. What are long-term implications?\n5. What solutions address root causes?\n\nFeedback: [customer complaint about service issues]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n1. Core Problem: Customers experience 2-3 hour delays in ticket resolution.\n2. Root Causes: Support team undertrained, no prioritization system, lack of automation.\n3. Immediate Impacts: 15% increase in churn, negative reviews on G2/Capterra.\n4. Long-term Implications: Reputation damage, slower growth, reduced lifetime value.\n5. Solutions: Hire 5 support specialists (3 months), implement ticket automation, \n   create escalation protocols."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nAnalyze each product mentioned in the earnings call transcript. Return results as JSON with:\n- product_name: string\n- revenue_growth_percent: number\n- growth_driver: string\n- key_challenge: string\n- outlook: \"positive\" | \"neutral\" | \"negative\"\n\n[Transcript of earnings call]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n[\n  {\n    \"product_name\": \"Cloud Platform\",\n    \"revenue_growth_percent\": 28,\n    \"growth_driver\": \"Enterprise adoption accelerating, multi-cloud strategy\",\n    \"key_challenge\": \"Competitive pricing pressure from startups\",\n    \"outlook\": \"positive\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"product_name\": \"Analytics Suite\",\n    \"revenue_growth_percent\": 12,\n    \"growth_driver\": \"Upsell to existing customers, new data connectors\",\n    \"key_challenge\": \"Integration complexity limiting adoption\",\n    \"outlook\": \"neutral\"\n  }\n]"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nSummarize the key findings from this research paper. For each finding, indicate the \nconfidence level:\n- \"Direct quote\" if it's directly stated in the paper\n- \"Inferred\" if you're synthesizing from multiple statements\n- \"Uncertain\" if the paper is ambiguous\n\n[Research paper]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\nFinding 1: \"The new algorithm improves accuracy by 8%.\" [Direct quote - exact percentage stated]\nFinding 2: \"This accuracy improvement is primarily from handling edge cases.\" [Inferred - \npaper discusses edge cases and shows them improving in ablations]\nFinding 3: \"The algorithm will outperform competitors on real-world data.\" [Uncertain - \npaper only tests on benchmarks, not real-world datasets]"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nCompare these two company earnings reports:\n- What financial metrics improved in Company A but declined in Company B?\n- What common challenges do both face?\n- What strategic directions diverge between them?\n\nReport A: [Company A earnings]\nReport B: [Company B earnings]\n\n---\n\nResponse:\nImprovements in A, Declines in B:\n- Cloud revenue: A grew 35%, B grew 8%\n- R&D spending: A increased 22%, B decreased 5%\n\nCommon Challenges:\n- Both face supply chain issues in semiconductors\n- Both mention intensifying competition\n- Both report slower growth in legacy products\n\nStrategic Divergence:\n- A is investing heavily in AI, B is focusing on profitability\n- A pursuing international expansion, B consolidating in core markets\n- A acquiring startups, B divesting non-core businesses"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Prompt:\nEvaluate this summary of the document against the evaluation criteria:\n\nSummary: [summary to evaluate]\nDocument: [original document]\n\nCriteria:\n1. Factuality: Is every claim in the summary supported by the document? (Yes/No/Mostly)\n2. Completeness: Does the summary cover the main points? (Yes/Mostly/No)\n3. Clarity: Would a typical reader understand the key points? (Yes/Mostly/No)\n4. Conciseness: Are there unnecessary details? (No unnecessary details/Some/Lots)\n\n---\n\nResponse:\n1. Factuality: Mostly - All major claims are supported, though one statistic is rounded differently than source.\n2. Completeness: Yes - All five key findings are mentioned.\n3. Clarity: Yes - Clear language, good structure.\n4. Conciseness: No unnecessary details - Each sentence adds value.\n\nOverall: Strong summary suitable for executive audience."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Iteration 1:\nPrompt: \"Summarize this earnings report in 3 sentences.\"\nResponse: [too technical, missing executive insights]\n\nRefinement:\nPrompt: \"Summarize this earnings report for a CEO in 3 sentences. Focus on financial performance, \nmajor changes, and forward guidance, not technical details.\"\nResponse: [better, but missing strategic implications]\n\nFinal iteration:\nPrompt: \"Summarize this earnings report for a CEO in 3 sentences. Include: (1) Overall financial \nperformance, (2) Major strategic changes, (3) Risks or challenges ahead.\"\nResponse: [exactly what the CEO needed]"
        ]
      ]
    },
